#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "bb2795c3-6359-50d8-9531-1e9dfae7a2ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-10994" :question/problem "Find $5\\det(A)-\\det(B),$ where \n![](images/65/65df227e4fff9e934cec11be0a0262a1093a82270f3c9b0b7970fa2c700151aa.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical columns, we obtain\n![](images/23/23865048a3c2ad60dd3b51fe78c44ee368692172300814c3fb061f447266e233.png)\n\n- Since $B$ is a diagonal matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\det(B) = 3 \\cdot (-4) \\cdot (-2) = 24\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5\\det(A)-\\det(B) = 5 \\cdot 0 - 24 = -24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/id #uuid "dc780837-b763-5ba9-981a-2373afcb524a" :question/math-academy-id "e-10995" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n![](images/d9/d95e60cbfa50178878e719166ace3dbff90c3cc5531acfc046d8354320cd4b00.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](images/3f/3f434912c97c20d04f703253fe41c169497cae82657cfbd0d8b548985549fe64.png)\nAs a result, $|A| = 0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, so \n\n$$\n|B| = (-1) \\cdot 4 \\cdot (-3) = 12 \\neq 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has a zero row: \n![](images/5f/5f41ff4f7fe5aeae5865bef9ab16d5d97a3513277f70b797c4167882093ed079.png)\nAs a result, $|C| = 0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/id #uuid "33ca37e5-c598-52a2-861f-2d5bfa6fd571" :question/math-academy-id "e-10996" :question/problem "![](images/cc/ccc50eec6218625f22e8372d6f0b1dbf0da0aa921dff237e4e1b8ea3761bdfc7.png)\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0.$\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows\n\n- $A$ has identical columns" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n![](images/2a/2a155f75e1e9c099540eeac555cb20fde5037837d9e5fc9f976bbca15369b51e.png)\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n![](images/14/1447045fa5b7875defffdf52d2ae8cf876ee0c5da6ac07cc37bc1c5525fec9c6.png)\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03dd7eb-af5f-5f22-813b-7f3d5b84651c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400869} {:answer/id #uuid "ab86d5e2-989c-5d49-9b2d-7a183fd53e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400870} {:answer/id #uuid "da8626ef-a38f-59a8-a718-2155b988e445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400871} {:answer/id #uuid "c0fe0f31-e9db-50f1-a23b-a66578e23d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400872} {:answer/id #uuid "1485ab74-1a6a-53e5-9aaf-e407a69b362d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab86d5e2-989c-5d49-9b2d-7a183fd53e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400870} :answer-field/id #uuid "d252fa00-ae50-5d73-8bce-ecc15224f399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400868}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c1bd5a4-43fd-5d63-843c-209b976b49d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-140046" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3} & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{6} & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 18 & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|A|=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 1\\cdot 4=8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has identical columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=5\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot (-10)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1321a890-eb6a-54ac-bf48-1d4c77ff2d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269436} {:answer/id #uuid "2417ace3-b1df-55bb-9e6e-f0cf724a7d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269584} {:answer/id #uuid "445c99d0-1565-5d0f-bd0a-b81957ffc9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269889} {:answer/id #uuid "b8d5f2c0-248a-5010-b938-a0307212261a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270902} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1fdb0e-edd1-53d9-ac51-6c3cbff27cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8d5f2c0-248a-5010-b938-a0307212261a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270902} :answer-field/id #uuid "6af39b6a-785f-556e-9462-97889783ccd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51a6e7e0-f39c-5b8c-9665-45f89b4bef77" :question/math-academy-id "q-140047" :question/problem "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4277cba2-c049-5ea5-856e-2ff6513db5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269868} {:answer/id #uuid "72da4e3f-61a8-5e34-b36c-55d3e99b038d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270284} {:answer/id #uuid "9abb2b39-bec9-5be0-99bf-81a5af073417" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270633} {:answer/id #uuid "9afef988-3992-5f75-bb57-47478f3265c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270637} {:answer/id #uuid "a39e8d77-7621-59cd-b046-86dcbd4ec894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a39e8d77-7621-59cd-b046-86dcbd4ec894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270727} :answer-field/id #uuid "f058dbfa-a132-5778-8502-105f66b5f7f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14e63fd3-62b7-575e-b489-4cda5c20ed53" :question/math-academy-id "q-140050" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43df28ac-2644-52fe-87ff-c9bbc61db0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327525} {:answer/id #uuid "799dc5a9-1369-54a6-a75c-e539a32dc0b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327977} {:answer/id #uuid "8773d6fb-f4f7-56c5-8a56-bc4991b94d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328099} {:answer/id #uuid "e8504291-e6c1-5fe6-b995-7a14a41fd690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328965} {:answer/id #uuid "ed4866e8-d417-50c7-9bc5-7abff6305bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329010}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed4866e8-d417-50c7-9bc5-7abff6305bed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329010} :answer-field/id #uuid "557553af-7827-57cb-bc67-fa9b18c0d56d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d571c31-8e0e-520c-b34f-482cf5518003" :question/math-academy-id "q-42458" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4731d43a-1037-5467-97a5-e798a96ef9d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327555} {:answer/id #uuid "658a8d30-d9af-5e26-83da-9719b1081d76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327818} {:answer/id #uuid "6d1056e6-0216-54a8-a348-f7fd16cd261c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327879} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4f71df-9ae0-539d-bc37-b9dfa1a2efd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328715} {:answer/id #uuid "f61627d1-d9a7-5fa0-8601-a797fc2e5d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f61627d1-d9a7-5fa0-8601-a797fc2e5d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329093} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ecac406-0aef-584c-9d48-0a6c47d439e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329307}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a804e446-7433-50c7-a8ce-2769d7a93237" :question/math-academy-id "q-42459" :question/problem "Find $4det(A)+4det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- For the matrix $A,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4det(A)+4det(B)=4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 0=12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1859d7c5-0d55-5273-a004-f8368886466b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415448} {:answer/id #uuid "4a61a420-d52d-5f1a-b48b-ade03dffdca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415453} {:answer/id #uuid "5fcc61bd-b9ee-5f9e-8558-651f8ea9c858" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415454} {:answer/id #uuid "851dc3ec-467b-568b-a964-3b5e34b3527e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415459} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e4e722-717d-508c-a98d-112f70b09d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415463} :answer-field/id #uuid "f920ea7f-06a7-52e9-8586-d0e6b44af6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e897ce2c-45dd-5cf3-9d25-ca84c0dd6ea8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42881" :question/problem "Find $3det(A)-det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has proportional columns, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0.57 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3det(A)-det(B)=3\\cdot 6-0=18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329700 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26501f58-881f-5efc-856a-b32d1ee8088d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327266} {:answer/id #uuid "608ea971-d78c-578d-816e-c8d8d9fbb167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327782} {:answer/id #uuid "87c21507-097c-54e9-98e0-37922d796fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328103} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a9e845-0b2d-596a-962b-345596d1f19f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328792} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2b8a36-70d0-56e2-a760-93acc609a76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26501f58-881f-5efc-856a-b32d1ee8088d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327266} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec99a44-6d87-5ca7-8efa-c3acfffc845c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28b8a89e-dee6-5589-be7f-d0c7386a7fd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42958" :question/problem "Find $2det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=3\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)=5\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0.17 & \\sqrt{5} & 4 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(B)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2det(A)+3det(B)=2\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402868 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "665b8959-619e-56ef-8580-a1cb1e4b9558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402870} {:answer/id #uuid "64b8f243-2c7b-510f-ba0f-db94cf33bd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402871} {:answer/id #uuid "d613850c-c563-547d-bf3d-1ebbc2fd8f08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402872} {:answer/id #uuid "0b3fe8ae-8e1d-511a-9447-a62e0e89b0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402873} {:answer/id #uuid "c240e8d0-5ba7-5ba9-9558-ad9c553e554b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402874}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b8f243-2c7b-510f-ba0f-db94cf33bd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402871} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d0cbd0e-5f98-5252-aa48-893e93a173fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56c75f73-8006-5c39-8150-6ad119a3d555" :question/math-academy-id "q-43058" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -\\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & 5 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a triangular matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|B|=2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 4=-40\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & \\sqrt{3} & 3 \\\\ -4 & \\sqrt{7} & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186415479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d00532a-c12b-50b9-ad0b-b9f1fa474794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415449} {:answer/id #uuid "44173bde-0fab-57de-b1b3-22d94262de8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415452} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9c1118-9a19-54c3-9683-cf1248dd342b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415456} {:answer/id #uuid "7e862f84-0fe3-5f4e-8829-b54fb65649ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415457} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9cd19d7-7290-5199-aa60-b1bc0b2d73b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80361a1-690f-54bf-a979-055f8bec64f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186415473}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f8a11ae3-b740-5975-a251-a4796d69b742" :question/math-academy-id "q-43307" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 3$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- $A$ has a zero column\n- $A$ has two proportional rows\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nExpending across the $1$st column, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-2)+(1-2) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither a zero column nor two proportional rows.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351408 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "28142e26-f6c7-54c9-9c16-035c75f7659f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b42c01-1203-51e4-be8b-21a9f39326a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348628} {:answer/id #uuid "51138293-d6f9-5d84-bddb-383e6734b677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349182} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1925ee-5925-5920-8f08-d4f72bb7c204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349295} {:answer/id #uuid "74c3f5d0-0ab9-569f-8ee2-928fd0331d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349519} {:answer/id #uuid "ac651b79-6add-5d70-bffb-99987c7c964c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51138293-d6f9-5d84-bddb-383e6734b677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349182} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1b6b7be-c0e0-5f4b-b713-96fc09be7392" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2eb579cc-338e-51a2-b3da-e05dcf5ef478" :question/math-academy-id "q-82286" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=(-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1=-\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has two identical rows: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=4\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-8\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ is equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133912 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8aef330a-81b3-56c4-9559-67df673e8687" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With Two Proportional Rows/Columns"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1436ec4c-88ce-5432-b5fc-bcc3977df9e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348619} {:answer/id #uuid "342c9e0d-3bc9-5d1a-8dd8-5ffecbcb9eac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348914} {:answer/id #uuid "6b821ea4-e43b-587c-b76b-a99bc45b8052" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349435} {:answer/id #uuid "81799b75-c13d-51a1-8f2d-733e3a588cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349640} {:answer/id #uuid "bd651af3-ee69-50d4-93e1-b295f7f633b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|A|$ and $|B|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1436ec4c-88ce-5432-b5fc-bcc3977df9e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$|B|$ and $|C|$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348619} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5128805-4f2a-5632-93d8-b430aa5f4d2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350986}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dec8cece-e79e-5652-812a-3c79c57417e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-82289" :question/problem "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is a diagonal matrix, hence \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 3=-24\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & -2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abaeea03-6a2a-5d37-a2af-a9ea109175ad" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Reasons Why a Determinant Equals Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b8fde55-e83c-5be8-a243-bc3e0d4f1b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348984} {:answer/id #uuid "4abdc8b8-7340-5441-8247-cd9710e6d8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349128} {:answer/id #uuid "5e840f97-66fa-5708-ac1e-dada9cd5903f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349314} {:answer/id #uuid "65ba8b41-d7c2-5423-aa89-3bf70d806ce4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349376} {:answer/id #uuid "ba050e08-5f23-5543-a117-9239f86d3514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba050e08-5f23-5543-a117-9239f86d3514" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350096} :answer-field/id #uuid "62635290-ba66-5211-8758-a27e4bc0bd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e8066ca0-5e8f-5876-924e-8be55bf1f74e" :question/math-academy-id "q-82290" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\n- One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n- $A$ has two identical rows\n- $A$ has a zero row" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we can make use of the following fact:\n\n$|A|=0$ *if and only if one of the rows/columns of $A$ is a linear combination of other rows/columns of $A.$*\n\nIn the case of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, this means that one of the rows/columns must be proportional to another row/column.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. For example, consider the matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe have that \n\n$$\n|A|=4\\cdot 3-6\\cdot 2=0\n$$\n\nbut $A$ has neither two identical rows nor a zero row.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."}]}
